<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/06N4">Remark <span data-tag="06N4">9.3.1.17</span>.</a> Stated more informally, Proposition <a data-tag="06N3" href="/tag/06N3">9.3.1.16</a> asserts that if $U: \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}\rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ is a right fibration of $\infty $-categories, then we can arrange that the functor $\operatorname{Ind}_{\kappa }^{\lambda }(U): \operatorname{Ind}_{\kappa }^{\lambda }(\operatorname{\mathcal{E}}) \rightarrow \operatorname{Ind}_{\kappa }^{\lambda }(\operatorname{\mathcal{C}})$ of Notation <a data-tag="06N2" href="/tag/06N2">9.3.1.13</a> is also a right fibration and that there is a categorical pullback square </p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix@R =50pt@C=50pt{ \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}\ar [d]^{U} \ar [r] &amp;  \operatorname{Ind}_{\kappa }^{\lambda }(\operatorname{\mathcal{E}}) \ar [d]^{ \operatorname{Ind}_{\kappa }^{\lambda }(U) } \\ \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}\ar [r] &amp;  \operatorname{Ind}_{\kappa }^{\lambda }(\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}). } \]
</div>
